# Probes the shipped C product gets wrong today, one per line:
# <probe> R13-0#NN P0|P1|P2 <one-line symptom>
#
# The product route of tests/difftest.sh (UA=... , see the header there).
# This is a separate file from tests/difftest.knownfail because the two routes
# disagree, and R13-0 is where that showed: fb12-03/04/05 fail on the product
# while the Python reference handles all three (the reference exits 0, 22 and 8
# where 0.0.12 refuses to compile).  One shared list would have to be wrong on
# one route or the other.
#
# Same contract as tests/c99.knownfail: a probe listed here may be FAIL or UNS,
# and a listed probe that starts PASSING is a FAILURE -- closing a defect means
# deleting its line, so the list cannot rot.
#
# Opened 2026-09-30; all six reproduced by dsh on the gate candidate df8cc9b4
# (the unsigned sibling of the shipped fb607af5).  Report:
# ~/unisacc-feedback-0.0.12.md.
fb12-01-printf-hash-flag R13-0#01 P1 printf: the # flag is ignored (%#x -> ff, want 0xff)
fb12-02-printf-hh-h-length R13-0#02 P1 printf: hh/h do not narrow (%hhd 300 -> 300, want 44)
fb12-06-stdin-is-null R13-0#06 P2 stdin is ((FILE *)0), so `... : stdin; if (!in)` fails on the stdin path
#
# R13-0b -- real-world batch, 12 projects (jsmn, crypto-algorithms, kilo,
# sbase, cJSON, fe, stb_image, stb_image_write, miniz, tinyexpr, Lua 5.4.7,
# SQLite 3.46.1).  Report: ~/unisacc-feedback-0.0.12-realworld.md, repros in
# ~/unisacc-feedback-0.0.12-realworld/NN-*.c with a .out.txt per item holding
# the unisacc and gcc records.  Every line below was re-measured on df8cc9b4.
# 18 and 23 are the release blockers: both exit 0 with wrong output.
fb12-07-missing-header-diag R13-0b#07 P1 a missing bundled header is a location-less run-time error, not a positioned one
fb12-08b-ulong-max-in-if R13-0b#08b P2 reject: not covered: #if integer literal (ULONG_MAX in an #if)
fb12-11-comment-then-continuation R13-0b#11 P1 reject: not covered: malformed preprocessing locations (comment then continuation)
fb12-14-parenthesized-declarator R13-0b#14 P1 parenthesized declarator is rejected
fb12-21-indirect-call-six-args R13-0b#21 P1 indirect call with six arguments is rejected (register allocation)
fb12-25-fopen-errno R13-0b#25 P2 libc: errno is not set on a failed fopen (ENOENT reported as success)
fb12-29-macro-more-than-8-params R13-0b#29 P1 reject: not covered: function-like macro invocation with more than 8 parameters
fb12-31-unused-static-refs-undefined R13-0b#31 P1 unused static references are reported as undefined functions
